<article class="env-example" id="0FUJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FUJ">Example <span data-tag="0FUJ">50.10.6</span>.</a> Lemma <a href="/tag/0FUI" data-tag="0FUI">50.10.5</a> is false in positive characteristic. The de Rham complex of $\mathbf{A}^1_ k = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k[x])$ over a field $k$ looks like a direct sum </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  k \oplus \bigoplus \nolimits _{n \geq 1} (k \cdot t^ n \xrightarrow {n} k \cdot t^{n - 1} \text{d}t)  \]
</div>
  <p> Hence if the characteristic of $k$ is $p > 0$, then we see that both $H^0_{dR}(\mathbf{A}^1_ k/k)$ and $H^1_{dR}(\mathbf{A}^1_ k/k)$ are infinite dimensional over $k$. </p>
</article>